@oct22_coal
# prose-audit: Grade C — The queues, the import ban that caused them and the municipal distribution law are staged with three answers that separate delivery from blame; the people sleeping in the queues are described rather than heard.
title: Queues at the coal yard
subtitle: A winter fuel shortage is handed to the municipalities to solve
face-image: img/poland/events/turow-mine-2021.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.oct22_coal_done = 1;
Q.household_security = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.household_security) || 45) - 6
);
Q.energy_security = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.energy_security) || 45) - 4
);
Q.administrative_capacity = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.administrative_capacity) || 0) - 3
);
Q.news_headline =
    "Households queue overnight for coal as the government hands distribution to communes";
!}

= October 2022 — The state discovers it has no coal counter

Roughly sixty per cent of Polish houses are heated by solid fuel and most of
them burn coal. The government banned Russian imports in April, which was
right, and did not replace the volume, which was not a decision anybody
admits making. By October the yards are empty, the price has roughly tripled,
and people are sleeping in cars in queues that form the night before a
delivery.

The answer arrives as a statute at the end of the month: communes are to buy
coal from state importers at a capped price and sell it on to residents. Every
mayor in the country is now a fuel merchant, with no warehouse, no scales, no
staff and a legal liability for the quality of what they hand over.

It is a state-capacity failure being solved by transferring it to the level of
government with the least capacity of all — and, not coincidentally, the level
run mostly by the opposition.

[? if reparations_stance = "Named as domestic instrument": Having spent
September saying the reparations note was a distraction from the energy
crisis, we now have the crisis in a photograph.?]
[? if nik_referral_channel = 1: The audit chamber can be asked to establish who
decided not to replace the banned volume, and when.?]
[? if local_network >= 30: Our own councillors and local organisers are in the
communes that have to run this, which means we hear about it before the
ministry does.?]

- @coal22_deliver
- @coal22_audit
- @coal22_blame

@coal22_deliver
title: Make the municipal scheme workable and get the fuel moved
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Helps a government scheme succeed and lets it take the credit.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party has no capacity to staff a national municipal support effort.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources = (Number(Q.resources) || 0) - 1;
Q.coal_2022_stance = "Made the scheme work";
Q.household_security = (Number(Q.household_security) || 39) + 6;
Q.administrative_capacity =
    (Number(Q.administrative_capacity) || 0) + 3;
Q.local_network = (Number(Q.local_network) || 0) + 5;
Q.rural_support = (Number(Q.rural_support) || 0) + 4;
Q.pensioner_support = (Number(Q.pensioner_support) || 0) + 3;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 3;
Q.labor_credibility = (Number(Q.labor_credibility) || 0) + 3;
Q.left_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.05;
Q.news_headline =
    "Left councillors write the delivery model the ministry never sent";
!}

Our councillors and organisers do the unglamorous thing: a shared model for
ordering, storing, weighing and prioritising — pensioners and households with
small children first — circulated to every commune that will take it,
including the ones run by PiS.

People get coal. The government announces the scheme's success. In four
hundred communes the people who made it work are ours, and they are still
there at the local elections, which is a slower and better return than a week
of headlines.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@coal22_audit
title: Have the audit chamber establish who decided not to replace the volume
subtitle: Requires an audit channel. Finds the decision rather than the queue.
choose-if: nik_referral_channel = 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no channel into the Supreme Audit Office, and the import decisions sit inside a state company and two ministries.
on-arrival: {!
Q.coal_2022_stance = "Audit referral";
Q.nik_government_hostility =
    (Number(Q.nik_government_hostility) || 20) + 8;
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 5;
Q.administrative_reform_pressure =
    (Number(Q.administrative_reform_pressure) || 0) + 5;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 3;
Q.state_company_governance_pressure =
    (Number(Q.state_company_governance_pressure) || 0) + 8;
Q.pis_relation = (Number(Q.pis_relation) || 0) - 5;
Q.news_headline =
    "Auditors are asked who was responsible for replacing the banned coal";
!}

The referral is narrow: the import ban was announced in April, the shortfall
was known by June, and somebody was responsible for the tonnage between those
dates. Which office, which meeting, which decision.

The chamber's finding arrives in the spring, long after the winter it
describes. It is the document that makes the next energy decision harder to
take casually, and the reason the phrase *state capacity* enters Polish
political argument attached to something people personally queued for.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@coal22_blame
title: Photograph the queues and make them the government's portrait
subtitle: The most effective image of the winter; it leaves every commune to manage the scheme alone.
on-arrival: {!
Q.coal_2022_stance = "Queue campaign";
Q.left_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.2;
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 3;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 1;
Q.pis_relation = (Number(Q.pis_relation) || 0) - 7;
Q.household_security = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.household_security) || 39) - 2
);
Q.covid_anti_system_pressure =
    (Number(Q.covid_anti_system_pressure) || 0) + 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "The coal queues become the opposition's picture of the winter";
!}

Cars in a line at four in the morning, a woman with a wheelbarrow, an empty
yard. Seven years of announcements about sovereignty and energy security end
in a photograph anybody can understand, and we make sure everybody sees it.

The photograph does not warm anybody. The communes still have to run the
scheme, they get no model from us, and a fair number of the people in that
queue conclude not that the government failed but that the entire political
class is useless — a conclusion with an address, and it is not ours.

- @poland_hub: Continue
